The topology would be very similar to that of the Universe, in which
all points appear to be the center.

Consider a person confined to move in 2 dimensions.  Place that person
on the surface of a uniform sphere (call it their Universe).  In all
directions, that person sees a equal amount of terrain, so they think
they must be at the center.  Said person goes for a short walk, then
notices that it still looks like there is an equal amount of terrain
in all directions.  "How strange!  No matter where I go, I'm still at
the center of the universe!"

Our Universe is thought to be very similar to that, with added
dimensions.

So, the nethack analogue is that, to every nethacker, it appears as
though the wrath/favor of the RNG is directed squarely at themselves. 
In reality, it is directed equally to all players uniformly, giving
the impression to all that they are the sole focus of the RNGs
attention.

How's that for a quasi-scientific model? ;)
